# SPDX-License-Identifier: CC-BY-SA-4.0
# NB: This document has been produced using GenAI
#
# The T-Box of the knowledge index (ADR-A134 decisions 4 to 7).
#
# This describes THIS REPOSITORY, not the insurance domain. It is deliberately outside ontology/
# and outside the substrate release of ADR-A129, and the `dev` path segment marks that. Only this
# repository consumes it, so changes are additive and there is no compatibility promise.
#
# ADR-A134 decision 6 is the rule that keeps that freedom honest: a class or property enters here
# only when a query or a check needs it. Every term below names the query or check that earns it.
# A term with no such line does not belong here.
#
# ADR-A134 decision 7: a DECLARED edge, which a document states, and a DERIVED edge, which is
# inferred from two identifiers appearing together, are different properties. SHACL constraints
# read only declared edges. The one derived property is `ki:citedWith`, marked as such.

@prefix ki:   <https://www.nebularis.org/neuro-semantic/lattice/dev/knowledge#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<https://www.nebularis.org/neuro-semantic/lattice/dev/knowledge>
    rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "LATTICE knowledge index vocabulary" ;
    rdfs:comment "The node kinds and relations of the index over this repository's working documents. Outside the substrate release, consumed only by this repository's own tooling." ;
    owl:versionInfo "0.1.0" ;
    owl:imports <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core> .

#################################################################
#    Nodes
#################################################################

ki:Node
    rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "node" ;
    rdfs:comment "Anything with a stable identifier, a one-sentence claim and a pointer into the document that defines it. The index holds no content of its own, so a node is a handle on prose rather than a copy of it (ADR-A134 decisions 1 and 3)." .

# The kinds. Each is a subclass because a query selects by kind ("every pattern tagged
# append-only-log") and because the SHACL suite constrains kinds differently: a principle needs
# evidence, a pattern needs a cost, a mechanism needs a pointer into something that exists.

ki:Decision
    rdf:type owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf ki:Node ; rdfs:label "decision" ;
    rdfs:comment "An architecture decision record. Earns its class from the check that no Accepted decision depends on a Proposed one." .

ki:PendingDecision
    rdf:type owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf ki:Node ; rdfs:label "pending decision" ;
    rdfs:comment "A decision that matters and cannot be made yet. Earns its class from the query for what a slice is waiting on, and because its definition is removable where a decision's is not." .

ki:Debt
    rdf:type owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf ki:Node ; rdfs:label "technical debt" ;
    rdfs:comment "A shortfall in something that exists, with no planned home. Removable, like a pending decision." .

ki:Discovery
    rdf:type owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf ki:Node ; rdfs:label "discovery" ;
    rdfs:comment "Something found out by probing, measuring or being surprised. Earns its class from the check that a principle has supporting evidence, which is a query for discoveries." .

ki:Rule
    rdf:type owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf ki:Node ; rdfs:label "rule" ;
    rdfs:comment "Prescriptive guidance an agent must follow within a stated scope. Earns its class from the query that replaces a 'go and read the guide' instruction in agent guidance." .

ki:Pattern
    rdf:type owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf ki:Node ; rdfs:label "pattern" ;
    rdfs:comment "A named, reusable technique with a trade-off. Earns its class from the check that a pattern states a cost as well as a benefit." .

ki:Mechanism
    rdf:type owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf ki:Node ; rdfs:label "mechanism" ;
    rdfs:comment "Something the project already has, described at the altitude of a design concept rather than a code symbol. Earns its class from the query that answers 'does this already exist', which is the error this index exists to prevent." .

ki:Principle
    rdf:type owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf ki:Node ; rdfs:label "principle" ;
    rdfs:comment "A durable design commitment. Earns its class from the check that every principle has at least one discovery or benchmark supporting it, so an opinion cannot be promoted to a principle." .

ki:Epic
    rdf:type owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf ki:Node ; rdfs:label "epic" ;
    rdfs:comment "A unit of work with its own plan. Earns its class from the check that every slice names its epic." .

ki:Slice
    rdf:type owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf ki:Node ; rdfs:label "slice" ;
    rdfs:comment "A deliverable step of an epic. Earns its class from the blast-radius query, which is what a slice reaches." .

ki:Question
    rdf:type owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf ki:Node ; rdfs:label "question" ;
    rdfs:comment "A design question raised against a slice, answered by a decision. Earns its class from the query for the questions a decision answers." .

# Things a node points at, which are not themselves nodes because they carry no claim.

ki:Document
    rdf:type owl:Class ; rdfs:label "document" ;
    rdfs:comment "A tracked file that defines nodes. Earns its class from the query that goes the other way, from a document to what it defines, which is how an agent editing a file learns what depends on it." .

ki:Term
    rdf:type owl:Class ; rdfs:label "term" ;
    rdfs:comment "A class, property or vocabulary concept an ontology module declares, summarised with its label, owner and source line. Earns its class from the query that answers 'does this already exist' over 3,049 declared terms without reading 270 documents, which is the error class the index exists to prevent. Not a ki:Node, because it carries no claim of its own: the module's own documentation is the claim." .

ki:declaredAs
    rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain ki:Term ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:label "declared as" ;
    rdfs:comment "What the module declared the term to be, as written, for example owl:Class or skos:Concept. Earns its place from the term query, which has to distinguish a class from a property before an agent can tell whether a mechanism is the one it needs." .

ki:Module
    rdf:type owl:Class ; rdfs:label "module" ;
    rdfs:comment "An ontology layer, standalone module or tool package, as repository-catalogue.md names it. The catalogue stays the source and this is read from it, never restated (ADR-A134 decision 2)." .

#################################################################
#    Status, as typed individuals rather than fifteen strings
#################################################################

ki:Status
    rdf:type owl:Class ; rdfs:label "status" ;
    rdfs:comment "The lifecycle state of a node. A typed individual rather than free text, because the check that no Accepted decision depends on a Proposed one cannot compare prose (ADR-A134 decision 5). The closed set below replaces the roughly fifteen distinct Status line shapes measured across the 120 decisions." .

ki:Proposed    rdf:type ki:Status ; rdfs:label "proposed" .
ki:Accepted    rdf:type ki:Status ; rdfs:label "accepted" .
ki:Published   rdf:type ki:Status ; rdfs:label "published" .
ki:Superseded  rdf:type ki:Status ; rdfs:label "superseded" .
ki:Rejected    rdf:type ki:Status ; rdfs:label "rejected" .
ki:Open        rdf:type ki:Status ; rdfs:label "open" ;
    rdfs:comment "A register entry or question still live." .
ki:Rehomed     rdf:type ki:Status ; rdfs:label "rehomed" ;
    rdfs:comment "A register entry a plan has taken on, so its row is removed. Measured: 26 such references exist, and they are rehomings rather than broken links." .
ki:Deferred    rdf:type ki:Status ; rdfs:label "deferred" .
ki:Complete    rdf:type ki:Status ; rdfs:label "complete" .
ki:Withdrawn   rdf:type ki:Status ; rdfs:label "withdrawn" .

#################################################################
#    What every node carries
#################################################################

ki:identifier
    rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain ki:Node ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:label "identifier" ;
    rdfs:comment "The canonical spelling, which is the one its definition uses. A mention resolves on a normalised key of letters and digits, because one identifier has several spellings in this corpus (tools/knowledge/identifiers.py)." .

ki:claim
    rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain ki:Node ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:label "claim" ;
    rdfs:comment "One sentence, at most 200 characters, extracted from the bolded lead sentence of the Markdown entry and never authored twice (ADR-A134 decision 3). It is what an agent reads to decide whether to open the document." .

ki:pointer
    rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain ki:Node ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:label "pointer" ;
    rdfs:comment "Where the full entry is, as a repository-relative path with a line range. The index is a handle, so this is the only route to the prose." .

ki:status
    rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain ki:Node ; rdfs:range ki:Status ;
    rdfs:label "status" ;
    rdfs:comment "Earns its place from every check that compares lifecycle states, which cannot be done against free text." .

ki:definedIn
    rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain ki:Node ; rdfs:range ki:Document ;
    rdfs:label "defined in" ;
    rdfs:comment "Earns its place from the referential-integrity check, which is exactly the question of whether a mentioned identifier is defined anywhere." .

ki:tagged
    rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain ki:Node ; rdfs:range skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "tagged" ;
    rdfs:comment "A design shape this node is about. The property where the T-Box meets the SKOS scheme of design-shapes.ttl (ADR-A134 decision 5), and the one recall matches on. An unknown concept fails the check, so the vocabulary cannot fork silently." .

#################################################################
#    Declared edges: a document states these, so a check may trust them
#################################################################

ki:dependsOn
    rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain ki:Node ; rdfs:range ki:Node ;
    rdfs:label "depends on" ;
    rdfs:comment "Earns its place from the check that no Accepted decision depends on a Proposed one." .

ki:supersedes
    rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain ki:Decision ; rdfs:range ki:Decision ;
    rdfs:label "supersedes" ;
    rdfs:comment "Earns its place as the inverse of ki:supersededBy, so the query may start from either end." ;
    owl:inverseOf ki:supersededBy .

ki:supersededBy
    rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain ki:Decision ; rdfs:range ki:Decision ;
    rdfs:label "superseded by" ;
    rdfs:comment "Earns its place from the query for whether a decision a document cites is still the live one." .

ki:answers
    rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain ki:Decision ; rdfs:range ki:Question ;
    rdfs:label "answers" ;
    rdfs:comment "Earns its place from the query for a question's answer, and from the check that a closed question has one." .

ki:waitsOn
    rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain ki:Node ; rdfs:range ki:Node ;
    rdfs:label "waits on" ;
    rdfs:comment "Read from a register's 'Waits for' column and a plan's prose. Earns its place from the roadmap query, what is blocked and by what, which is today answered by a hand-maintained index." .

ki:partOf
    rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain ki:Slice ; rdfs:range ki:Epic ;
    rdfs:label "part of" ;
    rdfs:comment "Earns its place from the check that every slice names its epic." .

ki:relatedTo
    rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain ki:Node ; rdfs:range ki:Node ;
    rdfs:label "related to" ;
    rdfs:comment "A relation the node's own author stated, read from a decision's Related line. Earns its place from the blast-radius query, what a decision reaches, which has to distinguish a relation an author declared from two identifiers merely appearing on one line. Weaker than ki:dependsOn, which asserts a direction and carries the status check." .

ki:evidencedBy
    rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain ki:Node ; rdfs:range ki:Discovery ;
    rdfs:label "evidenced by" ;
    rdfs:comment "Earns its place from the check that a principle rests on a discovery or a benchmark rather than on an opinion." .

ki:supports
    rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain ki:Node ; rdfs:range ki:Principle ;
    rdfs:label "supports" ;
    rdfs:comment "Earns its place as the inverse direction of ki:evidencedBy, so a principle can be asked what rests on it as well as what holds it up." .

ki:solves
    rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain ki:Mechanism ; rdfs:range skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "solves" ;
    rdfs:comment "The shape of problem a mechanism answers, phrased as the problem and never as the mechanism's own name, because an agent matches against it before knowing the mechanism exists (ADR-A134 decision 9)." .

ki:ownedBy
    rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain ki:Node ; rdfs:range ki:Module ;
    rdfs:label "owned by" ;
    rdfs:comment "Earns its place from the mechanism query, which must say which layer or tool a thing belongs to before an agent can reuse it." .

#################################################################
#    The one derived edge, which no check may trust
#################################################################

ki:citedWith
    rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain ki:Node ; rdfs:range ki:Node ;
    rdfs:label "cited with" ;
    rdfs:comment "Two identifiers written on one line. A hint for navigation, never evidence. Untyped, so it cannot say whether one answers, supersedes or merely mentions the other, and measured to over-reach: 2,458 such edges exist, most of them through hub documents. ADR-A134 decision 7 forbids any SHACL constraint from reading it." .
